cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DeepReality: A Multi-Layer Forensic Architecture for Detecting AI-Generated and Manipulated Imagery"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kurtuluş"
    given-names: "Ömer Faruk"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmerKurtulus/DeepReality"
url: "https://github.com/OmerKurtulus/DeepReality"
abstract: >-
  DeepReality is a six-layer forensic architecture for detecting
  AI-generated and manipulated imagery. Fifteen independent analysis
  modules ("pins") examine an image from mutually independent
  epistemic positions — documentary provenance, compression physics,
  spatial deep learning, frequency-domain analysis, gradient-based
  explainability — and an adjudication stage resolves them under an
  explicit four-tier evidence hierarchy in which cryptographic
  provenance constrains statistical inference rather than competing
  with it. A calibrated gradient-boosted meta-learner provides a
  statistically derived second opinion, cross-checked against the
  symbolic adjudication.
keywords:
  - deepfake detection
  - synthetic media
  - image forensics
  - explainable AI
  - C2PA
  - content provenance
  - ensemble learning
  - CLIP
  - SigLIP
